# Yespo REST API — Products & Markets

Full documentation: `docs/yespo-api-products-markets.md`

## Endpoints

| Method   | Endpoint       | Purpose                                    |
|----------|----------------|--------------------------------------------|
| POST     | /v1/products   | Create or update products (catalog sync)   |
| DELETE   | /v1/products   | Delete products                            |
| POST     | /v1/markets    | Set market-specific prices, stock, URLs    |

**Limits:** 1,000 items/request · 10 MB max body · 60 req/min per siteId

---

## POST /v1/products

### Top-level envelope

```json
{
  "siteId": "my_store",
  "languageCode": "uk",
  "languageChanged": false,
  "products": [...]
}
```

- `languageCode` is fixed per `siteId` after first accepted request.
- Changing it without `languageChanged: true` → `409 LANGUAGE_CODE_MISMATCH`.

### Product fields

| Field         | Type    | Required on create | Notes |
|---------------|---------|--------------------|-------|
| `action`      | String  | Yes                | `"create"` or `"update"` |
| `productId`   | String  | Yes                | Max 128 chars. Must match tracking identity. |
| `updatedDate` | String  | Yes                | RFC3339 UTC (e.g. `2026-04-01T09:07:15Z`) |
| `name`        | String  | Yes                | Max 500 chars, default language |
| `imageUrl`    | String  | Yes                | Absolute URL, min 200×200 px |
| `url`         | String  | Yes                | Absolute URL, default language |
| `isInStock`   | Integer | Yes                | `1` or `0` |
| `price`       | Float   | Yes                | Base price, no currency symbol |
| `currency`    | String  | Yes                | ISO 4217 (e.g. `"UAH"`, `"USD"`) |
| `categories`  | Array   | Yes                | Min 1. On update: omit=preserve, new array=full replace |
| `oldPrice`    | Float   | No                 | Must be > `price` when both present |
| `brand`       | String  | No                 | Max 256 chars |
| `description` | String  | No                 | Plain text, no HTML, max 10,000 chars |
| `itemGroupId` | String  | No                 | Variant group identifier, max 128 chars |
| `translations`| Array   | No                 | `[{ "en": { name, url, description, categories } }]` |
| `tags`        | Object  | No                 | `{ "Color": ["Black"], "Size": ["M"] }`. On update: omit key=preserve, new value=replace that key. |
| `remove`      | Object  | No                 | ProductRemovePatch — explicit removal of optional fields, tags, or translations. |

**`discount` is ignored — server derives it from `oldPrice` and `price`. Never send it.**

### Update semantics

- Scalar: omit=preserve · new value=overwrite · `null` is **not** used for clearing
- `categories`: omit=preserve · new array=full replace · `null`=invalid
- `tags.{key}`: omit=preserve · new array=replace that key · `remove.tags: ["{key}"]`=remove
- `translations`: omit=preserve all · `[{"en":{...}}]`=replace en, preserve others

### Removing fields — use `remove` object (never use `null`)

```json
{ "remove": { "fields": ["oldPrice"], "tags": ["Season"], "translations": ["en"] } }
```

| What to remove               | How |
|------------------------------|-----|
| `oldPrice`                   | `remove.fields: ["oldPrice"]` |
| `description`/`brand`/`itemGroupId` | `remove.fields: ["description"]` etc. |
| One tag                      | `remove.tags: ["Season"]` |
| All translations             | `remove.fields: ["translations"]` |
| One translation locale       | `remove.translations: ["en"]` |

### Category object

```json
{ "id": "8", "name": "T-Shirts", "path": ["Clothing", "Tops", "T-Shirts"], "type": "category" }
```

`type`: `"category"` (hierarchical, default) or `"collection"` (flat, cross-sell).

